Revision history for Proxy-Impersonate

0.03  2026-07-16
    - Coherence: forward WebKit's real per-request Sec-Fetch-* + Accept headers
      (override curl's static navigation defaults) and strip Sec-Fetch-User /
      Upgrade-Insecure-Requests when WebKit omits them, so a subresource no longer
      looks like a document load. Requires Curl::Impersonate 0.03.
    - Ignore SIGPIPE: a client resetting mid-response no longer terminates the
      (in-process) proxy before the graceful abort runs.
    - Accept is synthesized to Chrome's per-destination value from Sec-Fetch-Dest
      (was forwarding WebKit's Safari-flavored Accept -- a Chrome/JA4 request with
      a Safari Accept is a tell; curl's static document Accept was wrong for
      subresources).
    - Chunked-body 411 rejection consumes the head + latches closing (no repeated
      411s on a partial flush); tightened SSL want-read/write watcher handling.
    - The Accept-CH host map is capped to bound memory on a long-running proxy.
    - high_entropy_headers => : high-entropy client hints (Sec-CH-UA-Platform-
      Version/Arch/Bitness/Model/Full-Version-List) are added per-host only after
      that host sends Accept-CH, matching real Chrome (and the JS ua_data).
    - Multiple Set-Cookie (and other repeated response headers) are relayed as
      separate lines instead of collapsing to the last value.
    - Bodyless upstream responses (204/304/HEAD) are relayed instead of hanging.
    - Fixed a per-session leak: the curl_multi<->EV callbacks formed a reference
      cycle that prevented curl_multi_cleanup from running (weaken the closures).
    - Drain the SSL buffer after the handshake (a coalesced TLS 1.3 request could
      hang); reject chunked request bodies cleanly (411) instead of corrupting the
      next parse; a client write failure aborts the upstream via curl rather than
      a reentrant remove; fixed SSL renegotiation want-read/write handling +
      write-watcher busy-loop.
    - response_head strips control chars (response-splitting guard); the CA key is
      created 0600 via sysopen (no world-readable open->chmod window); ca_dir 0700.

0.02  2026-07-16
    - Add shutdown(): in-process teardown that closes active connections and
      releases the curl_multi wiring without EV::break, for embedding the proxy
      in another EV loop (e.g. EV::WebKit).

0.01  2026-07-16
    - Initial release.
    - EV MITM proxy: terminates a client's TLS with a single persisted
      self-signed cert and re-originates each request upstream through
      Curl::Impersonate, so origins see the chosen browser's TLS (JA3/JA4) and
      HTTP/2 (Akamai) connection fingerprint instead of the local TLS stack.
    - HTTP and HTTPS-via-CONNECT; h1/h2 upstream; incremental response streaming
      with backpressure (CURLPAUSE); keep-alive for fixed-length responses,
      close-delimiting for unknown-length ones.
    - Companion to EV::WebKit: the WebKit side accepts the proxy cert via
      set_tls_errors_policy(IGNORE) and routes through it with set_proxy (the
      SSL_CERT_FILE CA-trust path was spiked and does not work on WebKitGTK's
      GnuTLS build).
    - Not in scope this release: WebSockets, HTTP/3 upstream, streaming request
      uploads.
